    "title": "Reproduction package for \"Committors and Reaction Rates from Trial Functions That Violate the Boundary Conditions\"",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21703984",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-31",
    "description": "<pre><code>Self-contained code and data to reproduce the figures and quantitative claims of\nPetersen, Lichtinger and Covino, \"Committors and Reaction Rates from Trial\nFunctions That Violate the Boundary Conditions\".\n\nThe package bundles the sliced_committor library, a vendored data-loading layer,\nand the AIB9 and chignolin (CLN025) inputs. It depends on nothing outside itself:\n\"make check\" verifies that the bundled library is the one in use, and \"make lint\"\nasserts that no module imports the authors' wider research codebase. \"make verify\"\ncompares regenerated results against the published values with per-quantity\ntolerances.\n\nVillin HP-35 trajectories are licensed by D. E. Shaw Research and are NOT\nredistributed here; the villin panels of Figure 2 require a licence obtained\ndirectly from DESRES. See docs/DATA.md.\n\nCode is MIT licensed; data files are CC BY 4.0.</code></pre>",
